# Codebase Memory

When working on this project, always use the `codebase-memory-mcp` tools as the primary source for understanding the existing codebase.

Before making changes or answering questions about the architecture, dependencies, components, functions, or relationships between files:
1. Search the Codebase Memory graph first.
2. Use the graph to identify relevant files and relationships.
3. Then inspect the actual source files when necessary.
4. Do not assume the project structure from memory when Codebase Memory can provide the information.

Keep Codebase Memory in sync by indexing the repository when significant structural changes occur.